From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: orangepi_zero2: enable the CE TRNG for kaslr-seed / rng-seed

With DM_RNG and the sun8i-ce TRNG driver U-Boot adds /chosen/kaslr-seed
(fdt_chosen(), booti/bootm) and, via BOARD_RNG_SEED, /chosen/rng-seed, so
Linux can randomise its base address and seed its CRNG early instead of
logging "KASLR disabled due to lack of seed". CMD_RNG gives the `rng`
command for testing the engine from the prompt.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@ CONFIG_SPL_SPI_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SUNXI_LED_STATUS=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SUNXI_LED_STATUS_GPIO=76
 # CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
+CONFIG_BOARD_RNG_SEED=y
+CONFIG_CMD_RNG=y
 CONFIG_SPL_I2C=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SYS_I2C_LEGACY=y
 CONFIG_SYS_I2C_MVTWSI=y
@@ -24,6 +26,7 @@ CONFIG_SUN8I_EMAC=y
 CONFIG_PHY_REALTEK=y
 CONFIG_AXP305_POWER=y
 CONFIG_SPI=y
+CONFIG_DM_RNG=y
 CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
